<TABLE WIDTH="100%" BORDER="0" CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" ID="Table1">
	<TR>
		<TD style="HEIGHT: 17px">
			<IMG SRC="images2004/GPContentBox_01.gif" WIDTH="17" HEIGHT="17" ALT=""></TD>
		<TD COLSPAN="2" BACKGROUND="images2004/GPContentBox_02.gif" HEIGHT="17" style="HEIGHT: 17px">
			</TD>
		<TD COLSPAN="2" BACKGROUND="images2004/GPContentBox_03.gif" HEIGHT="17" WIDTH="100%" style="HEIGHT: 17px"></TD>
		<TD BACKGROUND="images2004/GPContentBox_04.gif" WIDTH="70" HEIGHT="17" style="HEIGHT: 17px">
		</TD>
		<TD style="HEIGHT: 17px">
			<IMG SRC="images2004/GPContentBox_05.gif" WIDTH="18" HEIGHT="17" ALT=""></TD>
	</TR>
	<TR>
		<TD BACKGROUND="images2004/GPContentBox_06.gif" WIDTH="17"></TD>
		<TD COLSPAN="5" BACKGROUND="images2004/GPContentBox_07.gif" valign="top">

							Take a look at the features
							GuildPortal
							provides its guilds! After you've checked these out, be sure to take a look at 
							our <A href="testimonials.aspx">testimonials</A> page to see what the real 
							people who use Axiom Shift's community services have to say.
							<BR>
							<BR>
							Keep in mind that the features we cover here are only a small percentage of the 
							features that
							GuildPortal
							offers. Here we're focusing on the "standard" features of community hosting 
							packages, such as forums, polls, events, and rostering. There are <I>over 40 
								different types</I> of content you can have on your guild pages, and we're 
							adding more all the time!<BR>
							<BR>
							<B>Community Management</B><BR>
							<BR>
							<P></P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>No programming required!</STRONG>&nbsp; We've spent over three years 
									building point-and-click tools that provide everything an online gaming 
									community needs so that you'll never have to see a single line of HTML, CSS, or 
									server-side script.&nbsp; Of course, for those with techy types in the guild, 
									you have the option of using some of these elements to further customize your 
									web pages.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>The most powerful community management features</STRONG> combined with 
									the <STRONG>friendliest tools</STRONG>, and that's no exaggeration.&nbsp; 
									Compare our community management tools with any content management system on 
									the market, all the way up to those that cost up to $30,000 per processor, and 
									you'll know how GuildPortal became the Leader in Guild Hosting!<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									You decide <I>what</I> content you want, <I>where</I> you want it, and <I>how</I>
									it is displayed using the Community Control Panel, a fast, dependable and 
									user-friendly&nbsp;web application that runs on IE, Mozilla, Opera and most 
									updated browsers.
									<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Edit existing pages, delete existing ones, modify sort order and name. No limit 
									to the number of pages, or to the amount of content available on each page. *<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Specify whether a page is viewable by the general Public, Associates, Members 
									Only, or Officers only.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Provide images to use in place of "tabs" for page navigation. Supports both 
									Active and Inactive images.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Add one of over&nbsp;40 different content types to a tab, choosing whether it 
									appears in the left, center, or right content pane. *<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Extensive display options that allow you complete control over how content is 
									displayed.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Upload and have us host your banner image. <B>**</B>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><BR>
								<STRONG>Transparent and Ethical Pricing</STRONG><BR>
							</P>
							<P></P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									Three product pricing options: Free, $30 every 6 months, or $45 every 6 months 
									(higher price is for guilds who want subdomains, such as 
									myguild.guildportal.com).&nbsp; Base paid product works out to $5 per month -- 
									try beating that with GuildPortal's functionality!<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>No hidden charges, no bandwith metering</STRONG>.&nbsp; Whether your 
									guild has 60 or 600 members, you pay the same price.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									No "community chest" that keeps extra funds for itself.&nbsp;<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									While charges are handled by PayPal&nbsp;and are re-occuring every six months, 
									if your guild is no longer active and you forgot about the re-occuring charges, 
									we will refund your most recent payment&nbsp;if your request is made 
									within&nbsp;a week of the charge going through.&nbsp;<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>We retain clients</STRONG> with&nbsp;a superior product and superior 
									service, not by pointing at&nbsp;small print.&nbsp;</LI></UL>
							<P><BR>
								<B>
									GuildPortal
									Forum Features</B><BR>
								<BR>
							</P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									Images indicate whether a forum has had new topics or replies added since the 
									user last visited the forum.&nbsp; Features "Next Unread," "Mark All Read," and 
									other features you expect from a stand-alone foruming system.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Security is by guild security level, being Public, Associates, Members, and 
									Officers Only. People who do not have the proper rights to participate in a 
									forum do not see the forum listed.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Extended Security</B> allows for Guild Administrators to specify that 
									certain users may have access to moderate individual forums, without giving 
									them administrative rights to other areas of the site. *<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Forum View shows forum titles, descriptions, topic count, post count, date/time 
									of last post, and name of last poster. Also displayed are the most recent five 
									posts, making navigating to the&nbsp;newest&nbsp;posts easy.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Topics and all associated replies can be moved to a different forum with two 
									clicks.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Topics can be made <I>sticky</I>, meaning that regardless of activity, they 
									will always appear first in the sort order of all topics for a forum.
									<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Topics can be <I>locked</I>, meaning no replies can be added to it after the 
									initial post.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Topics that are hot, meaning they have a certain number of replies or greater, 
									get a "burning folder" icon.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Topics track the last reply and the last view for the current user, showing 
									different icons for topics that are either new or have new replies since the 
									last time the user viewed them.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Posts show the user name, their "title" as assigned by guild administrators, 
									the number of posts that the user has made on guild forums, their 
									"participation rating", and&nbsp;customizable rank images&nbsp;based upon how 
									many posts they've made.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Posts are editable by the poster or forum moderators.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Thumbnail images appear under the name of the poster.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Signatures appear under the body of posts based upon the poster's settings.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									A "mail" icon appears next to the user's name and, when clicked, incorporates 
									the messaging system to provide an easy way to send private messages to members 
									of a guild.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Forum Pruning</B> allows forum administrators to remove topics that have 
									been inactive for a specified number of months.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Mark all Topics Read lets users single-click to mark all topics within a given 
									forum read.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Share selected forums</STRONG> with other guilds in your alliance!<BR>
									<BR>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><B>GuildPortal
									Voting Features</B><BR>
								<BR>
							</P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									Voting polls are truly stand-alone, meaning you do not need to bury them inside 
									a forum post.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									People can comment on the polls available, if they have the access to see and 
									vote on them. *<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Polls can be set to allow votes/viewing by the Public, Associates, Members 
									Only, or Officer Only.
									<BR>
								&nbsp;
								<LI>
									Results are visible from the poll itself, and a&nbsp;pie chart is available 
									from each poll to&nbsp;provide a graphical representation of the results.<BR>
								&nbsp;
								<LI>
									Once a poll has closed (meaning the Close Date has passed), the winning poll 
									choice is displayed on the main Voting Polls screen.<BR>
									<BR>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><BR>
								<B>Web-Based Mail</B><BR>
								<BR>
							</P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									Tight integration with most other sections of the site. In most areas, if you 
									see a user's name, there's an icon next to it that you can click on to send a 
									private message.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									New mail notification at the top of all guild pages, with a flashing icon 
									indicating when you have new mail waiting.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Inbox</B> shows all mail waiting for you, with icons showing whether you've 
									read each message, a subject header, who it was from, and when it was sent.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Sent Items</B> shows messages you've sent that haven't been deleted. 
									Messages indicate whether the person you sent it to has read it yet and, if so, 
									when they read it.<BR>
								&nbsp;
								<LI>
									Custom Folders help keep your messages organized.
									<BR>
								&nbsp;
								<LI>
									<B>Address Book</B> shows all members of all guilds that you're a member of, 
									providing a central location to send web-based mail.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Checkboxes next to each item and a "delete selected" button to make cleaning up 
									your mailbox easy.<BR>
									<BR>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><B>Events Management</B><BR>
								<BR>
							</P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									Events set to Public, Associates, Members Only, or Officers Only to 
									view/attend/sign-up.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Date/Time appear to the user based upon their time zone settings, showing them 
									at what time the event occurs by their time zone.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Attendance level allows event administrators to specify five levels of 
									participation requirements, ranging from totally optional to mandatory 
									attendance.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Tight integration with the game your guild plays, allowing events to be 
									associated with <I>zones</I>, or areas, within the game your guild plays. If 
									available, links to external systems with maps for the locations are provided!<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Event Sign-up</B>, allowing participants to specify ahead of time whether 
									they will be attending the event, giving event coordinators/raid leaders a good 
									idea of the balance of people they'll have available for a given event.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Event/Raid Points</B>, giving event administrators the ability to reward 
									points for attending events.&nbsp; Integrated with the Bank content type to 
									manage awarding items based upon raid point standings.&nbsp; This system is 
									totally optional, and does <EM>not</EM> require that your guild implement a 
									raid point/DKP system.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Share events with allied guilds</STRONG> also using
									GuildPortal
									to host their guild's site.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Commenting available for members that have access to view the event. *<BR>
									<BR>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><B>Community Participation Rewards</B><BR>
								<BR>
							</P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									Graphical indicators for people who participate regularly, encouraging your 
									members to stay active on your site and keep up on guild happenings.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Post counts, titles, "stars."<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Participation rating based upon posts, event sign-ups, voting, and other 
									activities. Can be reset at any time the administrators decide to "level the 
									playing field."<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Top 5, Bottom 5 member content types that can be placed anywhere on your guild 
									pages.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Raid/Event Attendance Points, integrated with Events Management<BR>
									<BR>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><B>Guild Banking/Vault</B><BR>
								<BR>
							</P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									Categories of items custom to the game your guild plays, with custom fields 
									based upon the item type in the game (ie, Range may apply to Missle Weapons but 
									not to Melee Weapons.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Items provide standard fields for quantity, current location (in-game), 
									comments.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Ability for guild members to request an item</STRONG> , which is 
									integrated with the web-based mail system by sending requests with single-click 
									approve/deny for bank administrators.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Guild Funds tracking</STRONG> , with currency types defined by the game 
									your guild plays. Transaction history to track where guild funds go, what 
									they're used for, and associated comments.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Import items</STRONG> that others have already entered detailed 
									information for, saving yourself time!<BR>
									<BR>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><B>Rostering</B><BR>
								<BR>
							</P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									Standard
									GuildPortal
									roster showing all members of the guild, their access level, title, thumbnail 
									image, participation rating, and member-supplied field values custom to the 
									game your guild plays.&nbsp;
									<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Member-entered and maintained data</STRONG> shifts the burden of 
									keeping guild roster information up-to-date from a single administrator to the 
									individual members!<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Multiple views</STRONG>, including Event Participation and Flag/Key 
									tracking (where applicable to the game your guild plays).<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Tradeskill listing</STRONG>, where applicable to the game your guild 
									plays, shows who has proficiency in various tradeskills.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Detailed Character Profiles</STRONG>, showing game-specific data for 
									the characters the members of your guild play.&nbsp; Journal entries provide a 
									way for players to keep track of and publish the ongoing life tales of their 
									characters.&nbsp;
									<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Medals</STRONG> can be configured with custom images, or imported from 
									one of our pre-configured templates.&nbsp; Community Control Panel allows quick 
									awarding of medals to one or many members, all at once!
									<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Where available, integration with game publisher-provided rosters (currently 
									available for DAOC and AO guilds.<BR>
									<BR>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><B>Quest Tracking</B><BR>
								<BR>
							</P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									Quest categories custom to the game your guild plays.
									<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Specify title, category, and what the reward is for completing the quest.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Add, delete, edit, reorder steps necessary to complete the quest, providing a 
									summary and full walk-through.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Members specify which steps of a quest they have completed.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<STRONG>Import</STRONG> pre-entered quests to save time!<BR>
									<BR>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><B>Real-Time Chat</B><BR>
								<BR>
							</P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									Conduct meetings or strike up a conversation with people online with our 
									java-based chat.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									Chat client is licensed and java-based, providing multi-platform support for 
									all browsers with an up-to-date Java runtime (available from <A href="http://www.sun.com">
										Sun Microsystems</A>).
									<BR>
									<BR>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><B>Other Features</B> (<I>not a comprehensive list!)</I><BR>
								<BR>
							</P>
							<UL>
								<LI>
									<B>News</B> small and large versions keeps your members up-to-date&nbsp;with 
									the top 5 most recently added news items, and includes a built-in news archive 
									viewer.<br>
									<br>
								<LI>
									Fan-Fiction/Stories content type allows your members to enter and 
									edit&nbsp;stories, broken up by chapter.<br>
									<br>
								<LI>
									<B>Quotes</B> with random display.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Who's Online</B> box shows who's been active on the site within the last 45 
									minutes -- integrated with the Web-Based mail system.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Information Sections</B> to store things such as raid/loot policies, 
									membership request information, recent brags.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Links</B> to other web sites.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Embedded Pages</B> allow loading of a remote web page <I>within a page</I>.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Custom Text/HTML</B> content with WYSIWYG editing.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>XML/XSL</B> transforms will take a remote XML document and apply an XSL 
									stylesheet to display remote data withing your guild pages.<BR>
									<BR>
								<LI>
									<B>Over&nbsp;40</B> different types of content!<BR>
									<BR>
								</LI>
							</UL>
							<P><BR>
								<BR>
								<B>*</B> - Some aspects of this functionality <I>may</I> vary or be reduced for 
								non-supporter guilds.<BR>
								<B>**</B> - Supporter guilds only. <!-- END CENTER PANE CONTENT --> <!-- END CENTER PANE CONTENT -->
										</TD>
